# Dev Notes 61 — Runtime Event Log Store Backend Contract v1

**Date:** 2026-06-21  
**Branch:** `runtime-event-log-store-backend-contract-v1`  
**Repo:** `Main-Michael-Sparks/runtime-dev-repo`  
**Status:** Candidate staged for the declared metadata-only event-log backend contract scope. Assistant sandbox syntax checks, fixture coverage, worker import hygiene, targeted event-log backend contract smoke, and related action-event / execute-action mock regression smokes passed. No real-runtime test is required for this candidate while it remains contract-only and does not touch runtime wiring, worker/native, lifecycle, request settlement, or stream behavior.

---

## 1. Purpose

This branch defines the next narrow event-log backend contract surface for future durable action-event/audit storage backends.

The branch answers metadata/contract questions left open by `runtime-event-log-store-runtime-wiring-v1`:

```text
backend definition metadata shape
best-effort / buffered / fail-closed append policy vocabulary
runtime wait-mode vocabulary as metadata only
append error-surface vocabulary as metadata only
read capability metadata for durable/cursor/bounded-history fallback distinction
future eventLogStoreBackend identity without selecting a concrete DB/file backend
```

This branch intentionally does **not** make events durable.

---

## 2. Modular ownership boundaries

Preserve this split:

```text
runtime/bus/actionEvent.mjs
  action-event envelope validation/normalization only

runtime/bus/actionEventHistory.mjs
  bounded retained in-memory history/readback only

runtime/bus/actionEventSubscriptionRegistry.mjs
  live same-process listener registry/filtering/publication only

runtime/bus/actionEventReplay.mjs
  optional retained replay/live-join orchestration only

runtime/bus/actionStreamDeltaEvents.mjs
  live-only action.stream.delta mapping from injected parent-side stream observations only

runtime/bus/actionEventLog/actionEventLogStoreContract.mjs
  append/read entry and result validation, adapter validation, cursor/read-result shape validation, high-volume event policy only

runtime/bus/actionEventLog/actionEventLogIntegration.mjs
  optional runtime append handoff to an injected event-log adapter, no-op by default, non-fatal append failure observation only

runtime/backends/eventLogStore/*
  metadata-only backend definition and policy descriptors for future eventLogStoreBackend implementations
```

No broad event manager, storage manager, DB selector, or runtime backend selector was introduced.

