## 6. Policy descriptor details

`runtime/backends/eventLogStore/eventLogBackendPolicy.mjs` validates and defensively copies/freezes metadata-only policy descriptors.

Default policy preserves current runtime posture:

```js
{
    policyId: "event-log.best-effort.default",
    appendPolicy: "best-effort",
    runtimeWaitMode: "never",
    appendErrorSurface: "observe-only",
    includeHighVolumeEvents: false,
    read: {
        durable: true,
        cursor: true,
        boundedHistoryFallback: false
    }
}
```

Known append policies:

```text
best-effort
buffered
fail-closed
```

Known runtime wait modes:

```text
never
until-accepted
until-settled
```

Known append error surfaces:

```text
observe-only
operation-result
throw
```

Important scope note:

```text
buffered and fail-closed are vocabulary only in this branch.
No buffer queue exists yet.
No runtime wait behavior was wired.
No append error is made fatal by this branch.
```

---

## 7. Backend definition details

`runtime/backends/eventLogStore/eventLogBackendDefinition.mjs` validates and defensively copies/freezes metadata-only backend descriptors.

Default contract-only descriptor:

```js
{
    contractVersion: "runtime.eventLogBackend.v1",
    backendKind: "eventLogStoreBackend",
    backendId: "event-log.contract-only",
    status: "contract-only",
    storeContractVersion: "runtime.actionEventLogStore.v1",
    summary: "Contract-only event-log store backend placeholder.",
    capabilities: {
        append: true,
        read: true,
        cursorRead: true,
        highVolumeEvents: false,
        durable: true
    },
    defaultPolicy: DEFAULT_EVENT_LOG_BACKEND_POLICY
}
```

The definition validator rejects:

```text
wrong contractVersion
wrong backendKind
wrong storeContractVersion
unknown status
unknown fields
path-like metadata IDs
adapter factory fields
appendEvent/readEvents implementation fields
DB/file path fields
worker/tool/process execution fields
non-boolean capability metadata
invalid nested defaultPolicy descriptors
```

